<title>GERMANY: Deutsche Post resumes Burundi parcels service.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Post resumes Burundi parcels service.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Post AG said it has resumed acceptance of letters and parcels for Burundi.</p>
<p>The postal links, which had to be interrupted due to a bitter ethnic conflict in the country, have now been completely restored, a statement said.</p>
<p>Post will be flown from Germany via the airport of Maya-Maya in Brazzaville, Congo, or via Kigali in Rwanda, it added.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706;  Fax: 5017</p>
